abort.done:
{done}

ZHA is reloading `{folder}` now: your Zigbee devices are back in a few seconds.

xquirks watches the values of each installed or updated file for a day. A notice tells you if they look off. For a file that is not verified on a device yet, a notice may also ask you for a device test. To compare the values with the device yourself: Settings > Devices & services > xquirks > Check a device.

abort.done_zha_not_loaded:
{done}

ZHA is not loaded right now. It uses the changes in `{folder}` when it starts.

Once ZHA runs, xquirks watches the values of each installed or updated file for a day. A notice tells you if they look off. For a file that is not verified on a device yet, a notice may also ask you for a device test.

confirm.description:
{picture}{devices}

xquirks has `{file}` for it ({status}) but holds it back until it is verified on a device. {reasons}

**Offer high-risk files** turns on that option (Settings > Devices & services > xquirks > Configure). It releases every high-risk file held back now:

{files}

The change list then offers them and asks again before it installs anything. **Not now** puts this notice aside.

not_applied.description:
{picture}xquirks installed `{file}`, but ZHA does not apply it to these devices:

{devices}

A device on another custom quirk: that file wins. Remove one of the two. A device on no quirk: ZHA could not load the file. See the Home Assistant log.

misfit.description:
{picture}`{file}` does not fit the endpoints of these devices, so xquirks does not install it for them. A device that runs an older version keeps it until an update for other devices replaces it:

{devices}

Each link opens a prefilled report on GitHub with the device's endpoints and clusters, without its name or address. With it, a later version of the file can fit the device. Before you send one, look at the [open reports]({reports}): if one is for the same device, a thumbs-up or a comment there is enough.

confirm.description:
Changed since ZHA last loaded `{folder}`:

{changes}

Reload ZHA now? Your Zigbee devices are unavailable for a few seconds. A restart of Home Assistant does the same.

download_waiting.description:
xquirks could not download these files of the change list yet:

{files}

The change list waits until it has checked them. xquirks tries again every 15 minutes.

tuya_check.description:
The typed Tuya cluster of the Tuya quirk files failed its self-test on the zhaquirks version this Home Assistant runs: {reason}

It checks each datapoint value against the type of its attribute. Until it works again, xquirks installs and updates no Tuya file. Installed Tuya files stay as they are, but their devices may show no new values meanwhile. If a device stops updating, you can delete its file from the custom quirks folder and reload ZHA: xquirks offers it again once the check works. Affected Tuya files:

{files}

Look for an update of xquirks. If there is none, look at the [open reports]({reports}): if one fits, a thumbs-up or a comment there is enough. Otherwise please report it in the xquirks issue tracker with the xquirks diagnostics (Settings > Devices & services > xquirks > three-dot menu > Download diagnostics).

confirm.description:
{picture}xquirks watched `{file}` (revision {revision}) for a day after ZHA loaded it or the device got new firmware. Values of the file came from the device and nothing looked off:

{devices}

Please compare the values with the device itself. Your device test can make the file verified for everyone with this device.

